<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jeremiah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 650–570 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jeremiah was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> prophet in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> from the late 7th century BCE until after its destruction by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonians">Babylonians</a> in 587 BCE. He warned that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> would fall for its unfaithfulness and urged submission to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, which led to his imprisonment under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zedekiah">Zedekiah</a>. After the fall of Jerusalem he was taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-jeremiah">Book of Jeremiah</a> is attributed to him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jeremiah.jpg" alt="Jeremiah" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Horace Vernet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SA_160-Jeremia_op_de_puinhopen_van_Jeruzalem.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
